ripple-manifest.json: the @ripple-ui/svelte 0.8.2 release manifest, the one the npm
package Paw OS and the Ripple site render ships with. It is the release asset
(gh release download v0.8.2 -R qbtrix/ripple-iui --pattern manifest.json; asset sha256
bcca322d6ac8fa5732669642f1adb6405372054ca5c5d0304ed74c667b58b8ba, generatedAt
2026-10-28T15:31:10.672Z, 216 widgets, with the "waivers", "intents" and "craft" keys),
equal to tag v0.8.2's packages/svelte/static/manifest.json once examples are dropped,
with every widget's "example" removed. The server never reads the examples, and one
carries a sample Stripe-style key that GitHub push protection refuses. ripple main
after the release (d8c5d8b) adds math and mermaid to markdown's description and a
theme note to chart's colors; neither is in the npm 0.8.2 build, so neither is pulled.
widget_relevance reads "intents" and concierge_runtime renders rule text from "craft".

Refresh from a release:
  gh release download <tag> -R qbtrix/ripple-iui --pattern manifest.json -D <dir>
  python -I - <dir>/manifest.json ee/pocketpaw_ee/paw_bar/ripple-manifest.json <<'PY'
  import json, sys
  m = json.load(open(sys.argv[1], encoding="utf-8"))
  for w in m["widgets"]:
      w.pop("example", None)
  open(sys.argv[2], "w", encoding="utf-8").write(json.dumps(m, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False) + "\n")
  PY
then update this file and the pins in test_the_vendored_ripple_manifest_has_not_drifted
(tests/cloud/test_paw_bar_ripple_profile.py: _RIPPLE_MANIFEST_SHA256, version, count).
